# Applies to every process that imports matplotlib with MATPLOTLIBRC pointing
# here -- including the VENDORED peak-regulatory steps, which never set these
# themselves.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS RATHER THAN A LINE IN THE CODE
# ---------------------------------------------------
# matplotlib's default pdf.fonttype is 3, which writes text as Type-3 glyph
# procedures. Those are not selectable and not editable in Illustrator, Inkscape
# or Acrobat: the figure cannot be relabelled or translated without redrawing it.
# The requirement for this repository is that every PDF keeps editable text.
#
# The vendored steps cannot be edited to fix this. Their value is that they are
# byte-identical to the previous release's executed pipeline, and a single edited
# line would make every hash in vendor/MANIFEST.json meaningless. Setting the
# rcParams through the environment changes what those steps produce without
# touching a byte of them, so the provenance stays intact.
#
# 42 = TrueType with a Unicode cmap, which is what an editable PDF needs.
# (Identical to plotting.apply_style() in src/common/, which sets the same values
# for analyses 01-03 in code, where there is no vendored file to protect.)
pdf.fonttype: 42
ps.fonttype: 42
svg.fonttype: none
